Subject: [PATCH] stamp-p4: no false execmem warning on NOMMU

On NOMMU VMALLOC_START is 0, so the default execmem range fails
execmem_validate() and the kernel prints "Invalid parameters for execmem
allocator, module loading will fail" at every boot.  The NOMMU
execmem_vmalloc() ignores the range and protection and just calls
vmalloc(), and modules (esp32_sdio.ko) load fine (#12).  Only check the
range with an MMU.

---
diff --git a/mm/execmem.c b/mm/execmem.c
--- a/mm/execmem.c
+++ b/mm/execmem.c
@@ -512,7 +512,9 @@
 {
 	struct execmem_range *r = &info->ranges[EXECMEM_DEFAULT];
 
-	if (!r->alignment || !r->start || !r->end || !pgprot_val(r->pgprot)) {
+	/* NOMMU execmem_vmalloc() ignores the range and pgprot. */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MMU) &&
+	    (!r->alignment || !r->start || !r->end || !pgprot_val(r->pgprot))) {
 		pr_crit("Invalid parameters for execmem allocator, module loading will fail");
 		return false;
 	}
